node_modules/
dist/
*.log
.vite/
.chrome-profile-*/
storybook-static/

# Next 16 writes these on every dev start ("Generated AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md for AI agents"); the repo guidance lives in the root CLAUDE.md.
apps/docs/AGENTS.md
apps/docs/CLAUDE.md

# agent scratch hosts and captures, never tracked
.scratch/
.scratch-host/
# Agent scratch — machine-local. Repo guidance lives in CLAUDE.md, which is tracked.
# `.claude/*` rather than `.claude/`: git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT
# DIRECTORY is excluded, so a negation under a trailing-slash rule is silently
# dead. The glob excludes the contents while leaving the directory itself
# eligible, which is what makes the two exceptions below work.
.claude/*
# ...except the feedback ledger: it is repo guidance, loaded by CLAUDE.md's @
# line, and must travel with a clone. Untracked would not survive a peer's
# `git stash -u` — which is how a handed-over report vanished on 2026-09-15.
!.claude/feedback.md
# ...and settings.json's worktree.baseRef: CLAUDE.md's own "Isolated agent
# lanes" section calls it load-bearing for every lane in THIS repo — without it
# a fresh worktree branches from origin/main and cannot see the branch it was
# cut from (measured 2026-09-17). A repo invariant, not a per-machine
# preference. If this file ever grows machine-local content (permission
# allowlists, model overrides), split those into a second, still-ignored file
# rather than un-tracking this one.
!.claude/settings.json
# ...and the project skills. Real files live in the top-level `skills/` (a
# tracked directory, so they survive `git stash -u` and travel with a clone);
# `.claude/skills` is a tracked symlink to it, which is the path Claude Code
# discovers project skills at. Same shape the archived systemsketch repo used.
!.claude/skills
# wrangler local state
.wrangler/
# Reports: the page is tracked, the captures it inlines are not (Zach, 2026-09-07).
reports/media/
# Python bytecode from scripts/ (the desktop launcher writes this on every run).
__pycache__/
# Generated from git by docs/build_whats_new.mjs (`pnpm whats-new`) — committing
# it would let it go stale, which is exactly what hand-tagging stories would
# have done too. WhatsNew.stories.tsx (2026-09-17 - 2026-09-17, one lane) is
# RETIRED: Zach asked directly for the Storybook tag filter instead (see
# CLAUDE.md's "Story tags" section) once the empty-state story shipped with
# nothing wired to run its generator for him. build_whats_new.mjs itself is
# left in place — its git-derived "what changed" answer is still correct,
# just not currently rendered anywhere — in case a future surface wants it.
apps/storybook-basics/src/stories/whats-new.generated.json

# Vitest browser-mode run artifacts (apps/systemsketch's smoke project): a
# failure screenshot per test file and the attachment blobs behind them. They
# are regenerated by every run and name whatever was red at that second —
# evidence for the session that produced them, never repo content.
**/__screenshots__/
**/.vitest-attachments/
docs/node-editor-corpus.json
